# Project

- Test and run adhoc scripts in Docker (`./docker/`). Do not install packages on the host.
- Be concise. Technical, not product-style: `filter dr_5 > 20` not "picked 5 day momentum stocks". Specificity matters.
- Page changes: verify desktop and `/m/*` mobile.

## Git

- `main` is golden: never commit, reset or push to it unless asked.
- Feature branches: cut from current `main`; code only. Never commit `user_data/` (prod auto-backups own it) except on an explicit `*-experiment` branch, which is never merged or deployed.
- Work only in the existing checkout. Never create Git worktrees, clone/copy the repository into a new directory, or create a separate feature directory unless the user explicitly asks first.
- Before any commit/push/branch switch: `git diff --stat main...<branch>` — only intended code files, no deletions of `main` files.
- Never delete branches, tags or force-push unless asked. Keep one branch per purpose; say which branch is for what.

## Docs

Do not merge these. Read the one that matches the work (both if the change spans layers).

| Work | Read |
|------|------|
| Stack, ingest/update, tables, API vs db_scripts vs frontend, LLM pipelines, `user_data/` | `README/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| UI file map (templates, CSS, JS, component names) | `frontend/COMPONENTS.md` |
| Market brief pipelines (Benzinga, Px, losers) + viewer | `market_brief/README.md` (auto-attached by `market-brief.mdc`) |
